    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d39">

                <pb facs="0167" n="51" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg51"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/597.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Germany to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-10-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 24, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Liang Tung Yen, Chinese Minister for Foreign Affairs, now in Berlin, hopes the
                    United States will regard the danger to life and property sufficiently grave to
                    warrant us urging joint action by the powers with a view to warding off the
                    danger of selfish independent action on the part of any one of them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
